                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This is an interesting one. Free on Steam, it's a very retro style of game. I mean like actual retro, not \"I saw a pixel once\" retro. You could set up an elaborate scam using this game, a fake arcade cabinet and a time machine to collect money any time between 1982 to early 1984 and it would probably work out okay for you.\n\nYou play as two helicopter crew members, a pilot and a gunner. Right stick shoots, left stick flies. Two buttons for special weapons, one more button for \"screen-clearing bomb\". Get out there and rescue prisoners and destroy structures.\n\nBe warned, it's an INCREDIBLY hectic game that picks up fast. There are eight campaign chapters divided into three stages each, my game ended on Chapter 5 stage 1 as I could no longer quite keep up with what the game wanted from me. If I kept practicing hour after hour, I could probably win that one, but then there's stage after stage after that...\n\n...plus an endless Arcade mode. Oof. Yeah I know my limits and I've hit mine. \n\nSo this was both really good and really straining and the only reason I'm not finishing it is I've really got other things to play. Not bad for free.",
